        "Replay completion assumes scheduler fairness.",
        "The existing production property uses in-memory operation traces.",
        "D1 admission assumes valid samples, completing commands, and no external writes during the modeled decision.",
        "D2 probe admission assumes successful startup and completing probes, cleanup, and local writes.",
        "D2 sample validation abstracts numeric-prefix conversion and assumes completing commands, cleanup, and local writes.",
        "Emergency models assume completing record writes. Timeout models assume timer service and effective cancellation.",
        "The separate models do not establish a composed emergency deadline, confirmed termination, or durable publication.",
        "B16 assumes stable valid samples and completing local writes. Its production fixture covers only the low-space opening path.",
        "B17 assumes a completing guardian sample, local record, and stop request before benchmark return. It does not establish a composed deadline.",
        "B18 assumes effective command-group cancellation and completing local writes. Its eight-second fixture observation is not a complete production emergency deadline.",
        "B19 uses an atomic admission abstraction. The production liveness check and benchmark launch are not atomic.",
        "Progress models assume elapsed clock time and completing parent decisions. Atomic model transitions do not establish an atomic production admission or a complete deadline.",
        "B23 models cleanup client cancellation under effective signals and advancing abstract time. The production fixture checks refusal and local publication separately.",
        "B24 assumes signed 64-bit Bash arithmetic. Its finite model does not cover every input string or the two maximum-value production characterization cases.",
        "B25 disables age-only deletion. It does not establish a safe ownership protocol, space reclamation, Docker ownership, or a complete deadline.",
        "B26 assumes a sufficient final sample and summarizes pipeline outcomes sequentially. It does not prove pipeline timing, concurrent faults, or durable publication."
      ],
      "bounds": [
        "Carrier: two signatures, three blocks, watermark zero, and scan start at most two.",
        "Replay: eight events, indexed replay, inline singleton, and yield interval four.",
        "Disk: initial free space 7000 MiB, floor 4096 MiB, band 4096 MiB, and samples 7000, 8191, 8192, 8193 MiB.",
